        <groundspeak:log id="721443646">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-09-19T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6252216">hunthikers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP441 Peter Loughheed Provincial Park 

[FOUND]

Hunthikers were camping at the Lower Lake group site this weekend and made a detour after packing up to go visit the cap site. A quick find, cap is in excellent condition.  Great views!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681919503">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP-441 Peter Lougheed Provincial Park.  Took some effort to find this one.  Went down the  wrong road to start with and then had to backtrack and go down the correct road.  Got to GZ and spotted the survey post but still lots of snow.  Took a couple of big scoops of snow and luckily spotted the cap which is raised up just enough off the ground.  Thx ofth.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="600816652">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-05-15T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4883787">Kottbullar</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP441 Peter Lougheed PP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Came to pick up our cub from the group camp and went down to a familiar spot to find this brass cap. Answers have been sent!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="446371381">
          <groundspeak:date>2014-08-26T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1627351">petjo2655 &amp; mony</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;19:00 Yes, we found it!! At least one of all those caps in register: 

BCP 441 - Peter Lougheed Provincial Park.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We stayed not far from this place for two nights and enjoyed the beauty of Kananaskis Country. We were excited when searching for it, because it was something new we have never seen. After couple of minutes we could spot the pole and take a picture of the cap. 

The shore of Lower Kananaskis Lake was calm and we spent approx. 30minutes there.

Very unusual but so interesting challenge cache. So sad that I can not hunt for it anymore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Greetings from Slovakia and thank you for your website with nice statistics.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
